; Server environment reference.
;
; Every variable the server reads is listed here, so this file alone is enough to configure a local,
; staging or production server. The server loads `packages/server/.env` first and falls back to the
; root `.env` for anything not set there. Variables marked [shared] are also read by other packages,
; so they belong in the root `.env` (see the root `.env.template`). They are commented out here
; on purpose: a value in `packages/server/.env` overrides the root one for the server only, so
; uncomment one only to give the server a different value from the rest of the repo.
;
; Conventions: active entries are required (or required for a feature you will use); commented-out
; `# VAR=value` entries are optional, shown with their default, or [shared] and set in the root
; `.env`. [secret] marks values that must never be committed. Values are validated at startup by
; `src/environment.ts` unless the entry says a library reads them directly.
; `src/environment-template.test.ts` keeps this file in sync with it.

############
# Postgres #
############

; Connection [shared]. Required: set them in the root `.env`; uncomment here only to override.
# POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
# POSTGRES_PORT=5432
# POSTGRES_DB=accounter
# POSTGRES_USER=postgres
; [secret]
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
; `1` connects over SSL; `0` or unset connects without it (default: 0).
# POSTGRES_SSL=0

; Pool size: the most connections the server opens (default: 20).
# POSTGRES_MAX_CLIENTS=20

; Connection-pool safety valves. All optional; see docs/operations/db-connection-pool.md for the
; rationale behind each.
; How long a request may wait for a free connection before failing. Must be at least 1.
# POSTGRES_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
; Server-side cap on a single statement. Past 210000 (with the defaults below), also raise the
; idle-in-transaction timeout: the active and aborted ceilings are floored at this + 30s.
# POSTGRES_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
; Postgres terminates a session left idle in a transaction this long.
# POSTGRES_IDLE_IN_TRANSACTION_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
; How long an idle pooled connection is kept. Keep it below any proxy or load-balancer idle timeout.
# POSTGRES_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
; Leak-watchdog ceilings. Each must be at most the idle-in-transaction timeout minus two watchdog
; sweeps, or the server refuses to start.
# POSTGRES_CLIENT_MAX_IDLE_MS=240000
; Defaults to POSTGRES_CLIENT_MAX_IDLE_MS; never lower than it or the statement timeout + 30s.
# POSTGRES_ACTIVE_CLIENT_MAX_IDLE_MS=240000
; For requests whose caller hung up; never lower than the statement timeout + 30s.
# POSTGRES_ABORTED_CLIENT_MAX_IDLE_MS=150000
; Watchdog sweep interval (default: the smaller of 30000 and POSTGRES_CLIENT_MAX_IDLE_MS).
# POSTGRES_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_MS=30000
; Pool health heartbeat log interval; 0 disables it.
# POSTGRES_MONITOR_INTERVAL_MS=30000

###############
# Credentials #
###############

; Encrypts the per-tenant provider credentials (Green Invoice, Deel, …) stored in the database.
; Required. [secret] 32 random bytes as 64 hex chars. Changing it makes stored credentials unreadable.
; Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<generate_with_command_above>

########
# Auth #
########

; Auth0. Optional as a group: set all five or none (empty counts as unset). Without them nobody can
; sign in with Auth0, so every real deployment sets them. See docs/architecture/authentication.md.
; JWT verification: tenant domain as a bare hostname (no https://, no path) and API audience
; [shared]: set them in the root `.env` (the client needs them too); uncomment here only to
; override them for the server.
# AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-tenant.us.auth0.com
# AUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://api.accounter.com
; Management API (M2M application), used for invitations and user management.
AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=your_m2m_client_id
; [secret]
AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET=your_m2m_client_secret
AUTH0_MANAGEMENT_AUDIENCE=https://your-tenant.us.auth0.com/api/v2/

; Local development only [shared]: `1` lets a request authenticate as any user with an
; `X-Dev-Auth: <user-id>` header, skipping Auth0. Must be `1` or `0` (default: 0). Never set in a
; deployed environment. The client reads it too, to send that header.
# ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=0

###########
# General #
###########

; Client base URL. Auth0 password-set emails redirect to `<FRONTEND_URL>/login` afterwards; when
; unset, Auth0's default page is shown. Optional; must be a full URL.
# FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3001

###########
# Logging #
###########

; Server log level, one setting for Yoga and Hive: debug | info | warn | error (default: info).
; Production keeps info; debug adds per-request lines, for development.
# SERVER_LOG_LEVEL=info

; Green Invoice API client log level: trace | debug | info | warn | error (default: info).
; Read directly by @accounter/green-invoice-graphql (not validated at startup; an unknown value
; falls back to info with a warning). debug and trace log every request's headers (including the
; bearer token) and response bodies: local troubleshooting only, never in production.
# GREEN_INVOICE_LOG_LEVEL=info

#################
# Observability #
#################

; Hive GraphQL schema registry: sends operation usage to Hive. Optional; unset disables it. [secret]
# HIVE_TOKEN=hiveToken

; OpenTelemetry tracing. Optional; off unless OTEL_ENABLED=1.
# OTEL_ENABLED=0
; Required when OTEL_ENABLED=1. The full OTLP/HTTP traces URL, used as-is (`/v1/traces` is not
; appended for you).
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318/v1/traces
; Extra exporter headers as key1=value1,key2=value2. [secret] when it carries an auth token.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Bearer <token>
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=accounter-server
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAMESPACE=accounter
; Defaults to NODE_ENV, or `development` when NODE_ENV is unset.
# OTEL_DEPLOYMENT_ENV=development
; always_on | always_off | traceidratio | parentbased_traceidratio | parentbased_always_on |
; parentbased_always_off (default: always_on).
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=always_on
; Sampling ratio between 0 and 1. Required when the sampler is traceidratio or
; parentbased_traceidratio, ignored otherwise.
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=0.5
; `true` fails startup when tracing cannot start; otherwise the server logs it and runs without
; tracing (default: false).
# OTEL_STARTUP_STRICT=false

#############
# Providers #
#############

; Cloudinary: stores uploaded document files. Optional; set all three or none. Uploads fail when unset.
# CLOUDINARY_NAME=name
; [secret]
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=key
; [secret]
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=secret

; Google Drive API key: fetches documents from shared-drive links. Optional; those imports fail when
; unset. [secret]
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_API_KEY=googleDriveApiKey

; Anthropic API key: OCR and data extraction for uploaded documents. Optional; OCR requests fail when
; unset. Read directly by @ai-sdk/anthropic (not validated at startup). [secret]
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=anthropicApiKey

; CBS price indexes (CPI) sync from api.cbs.gov.il: a startup backfill plus a daily run.
; `1` or `0` (default: 1).
# PRICE_INDEX_SYNC_ENABLED=1

###################
# Email ingestion #
###################

; Shared token the email-ingestion-gateway sends as `X-Gateway-CP-Token` to authenticate as the
; gateway control plane. Must match the gateway's GATEWAY_CP_TOKEN. Optional; when unset, the server
; rejects the gateway and email ingestion stops. [secret] At least 32 random bytes.
# GATEWAY_CP_TOKEN=<generate_a_random_token>

#####################
# Runtime and tests #
#####################

; Standard Node environment name. Defaults OTEL_DEPLOYMENT_ENV, and libraries (e.g. Yoga) read it
; directly to pick development or production behaviour. Not validated at startup.
# NODE_ENV=development

; Any non-empty value silences dotenv's debug output when the server loads its .env files. Meant for
; deployed environments; not validated at startup.
# RELEASE=1

; Local development only [shared]: richer library logs. Libraries built on `debug` key their output
; off DEBUG, and some of it includes request headers and bodies, so never set it in production.
; Server and Green Invoice logs ignore it; use SERVER_LOG_LEVEL and GREEN_INVOICE_LOG_LEVEL instead.
# DEBUG=1

; Loads this file instead of `packages/server/.env` + root `.env`. Read before any .env file is
; loaded, so it only works from the shell or a test harness, never from a .env file.
# TEST_ENV_FILE=../../.env.test
